# Custom tag alphabets

A display alphabet changes glyphs, not tag identity. Create a live session
carrying a, c, and z, and configure Fraktur for its inline and footer display.

    :b jj cat (available)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s target-with-limited-name-padding "cat" (success)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag a target-with-limited-name-padding (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag c target-with-limited-name-padding (exit: 0)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --tag z target-with-limited-name-padding (exit: 0)
    :w fraktur.toml (written)

```toml
[ui]
tags = "𝖆𝖇𝖈𝖉𝖊𝖋𝖌𝖍𝖎𝖏𝖐𝖑𝖒𝖓𝖔𝖕𝖖𝖗𝖘𝖙𝖚𝖛𝖜𝖝𝖞𝖟"
```

    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth --no-base --config fraktur.toml; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 100 -y 10 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p target

The row and footer show the configured glyphs. Batch input is still ASCII:
uppercase B stages adding Fraktur b, and lowercase c stages removing saved c.
The right-hand overlay shows both edits, while the row keeps saved a, c, z.
C-t applies both edits. JSON still emits a, b, z.

