 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags: ａｂｄｚ                                                     ┃
```

Invalid alphabets fail configuration loading with exit 1 before the picker
opens: the first has too few characters, and the second ends in whitespace.

    :w short.toml (written)

```toml
[ui]
tags = "abc"
```

    :$ smth --config short.toml --json (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: could not parse config: TOML parse error at line 2, column 8
  |
2 | tags = "abc"
  |        ^^^^^
alphabet must contain exactly 26 characters, or a single character that represents the start of a consecutive range of 26 valid characters

```

    :w invisible.toml (written)

```toml
[ui]
tags = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxy "
```

    :$ smth --config invisible.toml --json (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: could not parse config: TOML parse error at line 2, column 8
  |
2 | tags = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxy "
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
alphabet characters must not be whitespace and must have non-zero width

```

A single starting character whose sequence extends past Unicode's maximum
code point is also rejected with exit 1 rather than wrapping or skipping values.

    :w overflow.toml (written)

```toml
[ui]
tags = "\U0010FFFF"
```

    :$ smth --config overflow.toml --json (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: could not parse config: TOML parse error at line 2, column 8
  |
2 | tags = "\U0010FFFF"
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
alphabet must contain exactly 26 characters, or a single character that represents the start of a consecutive range of 26 valid characters

```

